1. Setup kind local cluster
    - Install nginx controller https://medium.com/@vaklinov81/deploy-nginx-ingress-on-kind-cluster-23b7cfb5ce66
2. Deploy the app, dont forget to change in /etc/hosts
3. Setup argocd dont forget to change in /etc/hosts
4. Create helm chart
5. Create and deploy helm chart app and argocd https://github.com/argoproj/argo-helm/tree/main/charts/argo-cd
    - create the repo integration
6. Configure github actions with build-push-action https://github.com/docker/build-push-action
7. Install github actions runner self-hosted https://github.com/actions/actions-runner-controller/blob/master/docs/quickstart.md
    - Install cert manager kubectl apply -f https://github.com/cert-manager/cert-manager/releases/download/v1.8.2/cert-manager.yaml
    - crate github token
    - install/deploy runner using that token
    - Setup/deploy the runnerdeployment and bind it to your repo as configurerd
8. CD using argocdcli
    - Download by using this "curl -sSL -o argocd-linux-amd64 https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/releases/latest/download/argocd-linux-amd64"
    - move to this specific if windows sudo mv <downloaded binary> /usr/local/bin/argocd, then type argocd for check
    - Go to argocd integrate repo, create app, destination https://kubernetes.default.svc
    - learn the cli, argocd login <servername> --insecure --grpc-web --username <username> --password <password>
    - argocd app list, argocd app sync <app>